1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
I can’t tell my family what I want without feeling
ungrateful.

2
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:09,000
Private reflection you can correct before exploring peer
experiences.

3
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:13,760
Planned AI organizes themes; peer stories are optional.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,300
Prepared preview. No model.

5
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:20,600
A local example offers a possibility, not an answer.

6
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:23,200
Arjun says, Not quite.

7
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:27,605
He changes the words: it is his parents, and he wants time.

8
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,400
Now the editable reflection changes with what he said.

9
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:35,750
He wants time to decide, without advice to stay or leave.

10
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:41,795
Planned Muse Spark may organize themes to review, never
decide what is true.

11
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,425
Day four: one member wants time to choose.

12
00:00:45,425 --> 00:00:49,125
Another member sees a different part of the situation.

13
00:00:49,425 --> 00:00:53,725
Day nine. The host says, I can listen; I can’t decide for
you.

14
00:00:53,925 --> 00:00:57,925
Fictional historical examples, prepared and not live.

15
00:00:58,125 --> 00:01:01,725
Day sixteen: Dev's question still has no replies.

16
00:01:02,635 --> 00:01:06,785
Arjun edits one question; the exact preview changes.

17
00:01:07,335 --> 00:01:10,525
The alias and group audience stay visible.

18
00:01:11,035 --> 00:01:14,695
Private conversation and context are excluded.

19
00:01:15,135 --> 00:01:19,135
Consent is unchecked. Continue stays disabled.

20
00:01:19,335 --> 00:01:22,035
Nothing is sent from this preview.

21
00:01:23,135 --> 00:01:26,245
No provider is verified or bookable here.

22
00:01:27,135 --> 00:01:29,530
Arjun returns to the peer thread.

23
00:01:29,687 --> 00:01:32,737
He could leave without sharing anything.

24
00:01:34,187 --> 00:01:37,297
Maybe later keeps that choice open.

25
00:01:38,687 --> 00:01:42,062
Private reflection stays out of the group draft.

26
00:01:43,187 --> 00:01:46,547
Arjun chooses one bounded thing that helped.

27
00:01:47,687 --> 00:01:51,467
He writes about asking for time before replying.

28
00:01:52,187 --> 00:01:55,952
This draft is only for the fictional group preview.

29
00:01:56,687 --> 00:02:00,987
The alias is visible; private context is not included.

30
00:02:01,187 --> 00:02:05,487
Consent remains unchecked, and posting stays disabled.

31
00:02:05,687 --> 00:02:07,467
Nothing is sent.

32
00:02:10,187 --> 00:02:14,042
His takeaway and optional draft sit side by side.

33
00:02:14,687 --> 00:02:18,417
One helpful thing, if he chooses to share it later.

34
00:02:19,187 --> 00:02:22,992
The prepared example shows no real people or outcome.

35
00:02:23,687 --> 00:02:27,007
Arjun keeps the next step in his hands.

36
00:02:28,187 --> 00:02:30,872
Private reflection is still private.

37
00:02:32,687 --> 00:02:36,022
The Dev draft remains optional and unsent.

38
00:02:38,787 --> 00:02:42,767
Nothing is sent without consent. Arjun can leave it here.

